# Fixture for api_error_summary oracle (t_port_api_error_summary.c).
# One raw error string per line. Covers every branch the C port mirrors:
#  - malformed streaming response
#  - Cloudflare HTML page (title + Ray ID)
#  - JSON error object {error:{message,code,type}}
#  - JSON error object {error:{code only}}
#  - JSON error string {error:"..."}
#  - raw plain-text fallback (truncate at 400)
<html><head><title>502 Bad Gateway</title></head><body>Ray ID: <strong>abc123def</strong></body></html>
<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>Service Temporarily Unavailable</title></head></html>
{"error":{"message":"Rate limit exceeded","code":"rate_limit_exceeded","type":"invalid_request_error"}}
{"error":{"code":"insufficient_quota"}}
{"error":"Internal server error"}
expected ident at line 12: unexpected token
This is a plain error message that is short enough to pass through unchanged.
Very long plain text error message that clearly exceeds four hundred characters in length so the oracle and the C harness must both truncate it at the four hundred character boundary and produce identical prefixes even though the remainder would differ if not truncated properly by both implementations consistently.
